#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/lru_cache.rst:14
#: 53c6d8ee4e6741e9b00891c06295ec2e
msgid ""
"An **LRU Cache** (Least Recently Used) is a bounded-capacity key-value "
"store that evicts the least recently used entry when full. Every call to "
"``get`` or ``put`` moves the accessed entry to the most-recently-used "
"(MRU) position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/lru_cache.rst:19
#: 34d7640226ad4294b3aa97ba6fe8bf7a
msgid "Foundations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/lru_cache.rst:22
#: 9ec4099ef4dc40139d882f2e03566ac6
msgid "LRU Eviction Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/lru_cache.rst:24
#: 8e845c118a184e6b9945113e4f5dea94
msgid ""
"Entries are ordered from least recently used (LRU) to most recently used "
"(MRU). When capacity is reached, the head of the list (LRU) is evicted."
msgstr ""

